*Drawing to be made by the candidate: a large **vertical section (V.S.) of mammalian skin**, with sharp continuous lines, a title ("V.S. of mammalian skin") and label lines that do not cross.*

**Layers and structures to draw and label (from outside inwards):**
- **Epidermis**: the **cornified (horny) layer** of dead flattened cells filled with keratin, above the **Malpighian (germinal) layer** of dividing living cells that contains **melanin** pigment;
- **Dermis** (below the epidermis, contains the structures below);
- **Hair** (hair shaft above the surface) in a **hair follicle**, with **hair papilla / root**;
- **Erector pili muscle** attached to the follicle;
- **Sebaceous gland** (oily sebum) opening into the follicle;
- **Sweat gland** (coiled), **sweat duct** and **sweat pore** on the surface;
- **Blood capillaries**, **arteriole** and **vein**;
- **Sensory nerve endings (receptors)** for touch, pressure, pain, heat and cold, and a **nerve fibre**;
- **Subcutaneous fatty (adipose) layer** (hypodermis) for insulation and food storage.
